{"title":"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Adam and Budan are playing a game of Bocce. Each wants their ball to land closest to the jack ball. The positions of Adam’s ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, Budan's ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and the jack ball, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are shown in the diagram.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the distance from B to A?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2012 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a\">part b</a>, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d1626dd896fee92a14365a6cf113fe7d0bbd8222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6aaf77c5b97f6d30832b69a8a4c973438b3fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(image in original problem but with AJ and BA labeled as 25 and 36, respectively)\n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94e96e12eb0045067f3d4ea6b6cd1c6c35b0e78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BJA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c520f0b1a9101edb33bc8a9b8f7926cc74234365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BJA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> is a right angle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(triangle BJA with the labeled leg and hypotenuse)\n</p><p>Thus, we can use the pythagorean theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f8de0615b48d2a857882058c54c84b0d731713b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ^{2} + AJ^{2} = BA^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b528d750ef7fae8d3e68da2a1738f0ffecb0ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ^{2} = BA^{2} - AJ^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/46168ec4e7806b72037f91ebbd0d0b3c854696af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ = \\sqrt{BA^{2} - AJ^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d1626dd896fee92a14365a6cf113fe7d0bbd8222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6aaf77c5b97f6d30832b69a8a4c973438b3fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f226f31b60359c8f0ee06f00ea6b35d3d86951f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ = \\sqrt{36^{2} - 25^{2}} = \\sqrt{1296 - 625}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"266\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9e9165ca59c21e667956c7832fe3af444e7a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{671}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37f9a47996ebd53b17b44a33389124117855c8ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ = \\sqrt{671} &gt; 25 = AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79858652043c8623925bffb2080afc6123fac78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ^{2} = 25^{2} = 625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94febed08a1e398ea93df7231eb93bc9d346be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ^{2} = 671 &gt; 625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2f556ed4d1922b117d5fdbdd8cede861ff2005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BJ &gt; AJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, the position of Adam's ball, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the position of the jack ball, is smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, the position to Budan's ball, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the player with the ball closest to the jack ball is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4693416ade38c46e5e00e6959c6d3d4066f48748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{Adam}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1752/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4207/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.283      1 -total\n 91.07%   13.007      1 2012_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n 38.06%    5.436      3 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35640:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230532 and revision id 278092. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}